    ],
    "root": "Lead session: cloned cobusgreyling/loop-engineering with hooks disabled into an empty scratch directory and read README.md, LOOP.md, docs/concepts.md, docs/primitives.md, docs/refactor.md, docs/loop-design-checklist.md, patterns/ci-sweeper.md, the loop-verifier, minimal-fix and budget-negotiator skills, templates/SKILL.md.loop-guard, gate.yaml, .github/workflows/daily-triage.yml, loop-run-log.md, scripts/github-triage.mjs (header and exec call), stories/README.md and the cited stories, resources/sources.md, and tools/loop-context/src/context-manager.ts (types, defaults, error signature, similarity and checkCircuitBreaker) in full. Read git history for commit counts per month, bot share and the commit that added each story. Read GitHub metadata through gh api and npm registry metadata with curl. Fetched and read the three linked web sources.",
    "review": "Every loop-engineering citation in the note was checked mechanically against the pinned commit: the path exists and each cited line range ends within the file. The lead rechecked the code audit's decision-relevant claims by hand at the cited lines: no model or agent call in tools, workflows or scripts; loop-gate built only by its release workflow; required_approving_review_count 0; the daily-triage and star-history workflows auto-merge their own PRs; loop-pause-all read by no code; constant tokens_estimate and actions_taken; the loop-drill canary header; the skills/ fast path in fork-pr-gate; the unquoted action input; 11,690 source lines and 433 tool test cases; 14 release workflows with provenance.",
    "limits": "Read-only source inspection. No install, build, npx command, script, test or workflow from the repository was run. Test source is not a passing test result. Starters, per-tool examples, the remaining patterns and docs, and scripts/issue-bodies were read by search only. npm tarballs were not compared with the repository. Adopter claims, sibling repositories and open-spek/loop were not checked. README and story claims are publisher statements unless the note says they were checked.",
    "lead": "Wrote the Relevance to Waymark section from the Waymark sources listed under local_sources."
  },
